WHAT: Adds #[arithmetic(unchecked)] to CallData::len(), making the
calldatasize - base subtraction unchecked.

WHY: CallData stores a base offset; len() computes calldatasize - base.
This subtraction can never underflow because base is always <= calldatasize
(it's set from calldatasize at construction). The checked subtraction
generates uaddo/overflow-branch that wastes ~3 opcodes per call.

GAS IMPACT: -1236 gas total. ALL 20 benchmarked functions improved.
  math: -80 each (3 functions)
  governance/vote: -100
  erc20: -60 to -120
  governance: -40 to -100
  verifier/plonkVerify: -140
  escrow: -16 to -20
  amm: -20 to -60

CODEGEN IMPACT: Removes uaddo from CallData::len hot path. Since len()
is called during dispatch (checking minimum calldata size), every
contract benefits.

TEAM NOTES: Second Fe std library change in a row that improves all
contracts universally. Steps 15+16 together saved ~3600 gas across all
contracts. This validates the strategy of targeting shared std library
code paths over per-contract optimizer tweaks.

NOTE: In the original campaign, this step showed a merkle regression
because the rosetta merkle source was different. With consistent source,
the improvement is universal.
